      "head": "82624c64a0fa08bc1aa335db0225f7392722c1fd",
      "base": "8541937537890de079011dab119654b3d7a02074",
      "title": "Give DefaultProgress a single scope annotation",
      "body": "Guice rejects a class with two scope annotations, so `@Singleton` plus `@MojoExecutionScoped` on `DefaultProgress` broke every realm containing the 1.3.0 jar. `DefaultProgress` takes a `MojoExecution`, so `@MojoExecutionScoped` stays. The module skips tests, so this has no unit test.\n\nFixes #127\n\nVerified: issue reproducer and a probe mojo injecting `Progress` on Maven 3.9.16, 3.10.0-rc-1 and 4.0.0-rc-7, plus the probe as an `<extensions>true</extensions>` plugin and with the jar in `.mvn/extensions.xml` on 3.9.16 and 4.0.0-rc-7 \u2192 1.3.0 fails with `DuplicateScopeAnnotations`, this branch passes with one `DefaultProgress` per mojo execution."
    }
